{
  "manufacturer": "Toshiba",
  "manufacturer_slug": "toshiba",
  "model": "TOSVERT VF-AS3 inverter (RS485 Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "vf-as3",
  "short_model": "Toshiba VF-AS3",
  "aliases": [
    "VF-AS3",
    "TOSVERT VF-AS3"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Toshiba TOSVERT VF-AS3 inverters on RS485 port 1 or 2 with the protocol set to MODBUS (F807/F827 = 1); RS485 Communication Function Instruction Manual E6582143.",
  "summary": "The VF-AS3 inverter's RS485 ports speak either the Toshiba protocol or Modbus RTU. In Modbus every parameter and monitor is addressed by its hexadecimal communication number: FA codes are commands (run word, frequency), FD/FE codes are monitors and trip-held values, and 08xx codes are the RS485 settings. This map covers control, the main monitors, trip history and the port 1 settings.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 0,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "The register address is the parameter's hexadecimal communication number sent unchanged: the manual's example reads output frequency FD00 with the frame 01 03 FD 00 00 01. Parameter F800 has communication number 0800 (wire 0x0800)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "TOSVERT VF-AS3 RS485 Communication Function Instruction Manual",
    "doc_number": "E6582143",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://cdn.automationdirect.com/static/manuals/toshibamotors/as3rs485manual.pdf",
    "pages": "ch. 6 (Modbus RTU frames and examples), ch. 8 pp. 8-1 to 8-3 (communication parameters), ch. 9 pp. 9-1 to 9-10 (command and status bits), ch. 10 pp. 10-2 to 10-8 (command and monitor lists)",
    "unofficial": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "Toshiba's own download host refused automated access (HTTP 403), so the link is the copy on AutomationDirect, a Toshiba drive distributor; it appears to be the unaltered Toshiba manual.",
    "Every value is a single 16-bit word; negative values are two's complement.",
    "FE versions of the FD monitors (FE00-FE07, FE15 ...) hold the value captured just before the last trip; only a few are listed.",
    "Output current and voltages are in % of the drive rating (0.01 % steps); convert with FE70/FE71.",
    "Input and output cumulative power (FE76/FE77) are left out because their unit depends on parameter F749.",
    "The Modbus implementation is partial: function 03 reads one word, an indirect block (F875-F879) or up to 8 consecutive numbers; 06 and 10 write one word; 10 also writes the F870/F871 block and 17 combines block write and read."
  ],
