  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set F807 = 1 (MODBUS), F802 to a non-zero address and F800/F801 for the line, then power-cycle. Write FA01 with the frequency and FA00 = 8400h (bit 15 run priority + bit 10 run) to run forward, adding bit 14 (C400h) when the frequency also comes from comms; read FD00, FD01, FD03 and FC90 for status.",
    "minimum_registers": [
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 64000,
        "why": "Command word FA00"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 64001,
        "why": "Frequency command FA01"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 64768,
        "why": "Output frequency FD00"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 64769,
        "why": "Status word FD01"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 64771,
        "why": "Output current FD03"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 64656,
        "why": "Current trip FC90"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Set F807 (port 1) or F827 (port 2) to 1: MODBUS and reset the drive. Commands from FA00/FA01 are accepted regardless of CMOd/FMOd once FA00 bit 15 (run priority) and/or bit 14 (frequency priority) are set; that priority stays until cleared, power-off or reset.",
    "watchdog": "F803 sets the RS485 time-out (0.0 = off, 0.1-100.0 s); F804 picks continue, trip, or trip after deceleration stop; F808 sets when the time-out is checked. The manual says the time-out should be set so the drive stops on comm loss.",
    "quirks": [
      "Addresses are the hexadecimal communication numbers (FA00, FD00 ...), not 4xxxx numbers.",
      "A plain 03 read returns one word; multi-word direct reads are limited to 8 words and skip numbers that do not exist unless F830 = 1. Missing numbers read as 8000H.",
      "Manual examples: 8400H = run forward with run priority; 8600H / C600H = run reverse (C600H also takes frequency priority)."
    ],
    "setup": [
      "F800 baud: 0 = 9600, 1 = 19200 (default), 2 = 38400; F801 parity default even; both take effect after reset. With F809 (operation panel connection) at its default 1 = connector 1, port 1 is fixed at 19200 bps / even parity whatever F800/F801 say (likewise F820/F821 for port 2 when F809 = 2).",
      "F802 inverter number defaults to 0 (broadcast): set 1-247 for Modbus.",
      "Inverter-to-inverter communication (F806/F826) does not work in Modbus mode."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Emergency off (bit 12) and PID-off bits in FA00 act even without the priority bits set.",
      "Changing F809 (operation panel connection priority) can lock out the LCD panel until it is rewritten over comms.",
      "F806/F826 inverter-to-inverter settings are disabled on the connector chosen in F809."
    ]
  },
